Package: tornadoexposure
Type: Package
Title: Explore and Map ZCTA-Level Tornado Exposures in the United States
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Hailey", "Hansen", role = "aut"),
    person("Jessy", "Nguyen", role = "aut"),
    person("Prachi", "Sanghavi", role = "aut"),
    person("Kate", "Burrows", email = "kburrows@uchicago.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Institute for Climate and Sustainable Growth (ISCG)", role = "fnd"),
    person("Center for Climate, Health and Society (CHAS)", role = "fnd"))
Description: This package contains data and functions to allow users to explore
    and map ZCTA-level tornado exposures in the United States from 1996 onward.
    Data comes from the NOAA Storm Prediction Center Severe Weather Database and
    the Census Bureau. Tornadoes of every rating, EF0 to EF5 and unknown, are
    included. Exposure can be defined by overlap, by the share of the ZCTA's land
    area or residents inside the path, or by the distance from the path to the
    ZCTA's population-weighted centroid. A sensitivity layer uses National
    Weather Service damage surveys.
